WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.390
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.730
Let's go now from Nikki Haley, who is officially
running in 2024 to Ron DeSantis, who is not

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.640
officially running in 2024.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.969
This is super interesting.

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:15.719
Fox News interviewed Ron DeSantis this morning
and said, hey, what do you think about all

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:18.860
of these Republicans that are attacking you
now?

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.779
The main Republican who has been attacking
Ron DeSantis is Donald Trump.

00:00:23.779 --> 00:00:25.670
No mention of it on Fox News.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:28.500
Just they don't even mention it.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.240
What exactly is going on here?

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.980
I have an idea and I will tell you in a moment.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:35.130
But let's take a look at this clip.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:41.540
And again, when you see how every day Trump
is attacking DeSantis, how do you interview

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:47.390
DeSantis about all of the people that are
attacking him and not mention the main guy

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.390
who's doing it?

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:49.390
Look at this.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.390
You've come under.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.020
Speaker 4: A lot of incoming fire recently.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.770
Nikki Haley taking aim at you.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.780
Larry Hogan as well, the governor of Illinois.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.260
You know, from your visit coming up here to
Chicago, Twitter.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.120
What's your reaction to some of those attacks?

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.790
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.070
So it's already weird because, like, who's
paying attention to Larry Hogan's attacks?

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.890
Everybody's paying attention to Trump's attacks.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:15.360
Speaker 5: Well, Lisa, you know, if you're
if you're an office holder and you're just

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.740
sitting there twiddling your thumbs and not
getting anything done, no one ever says anything,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.400
you can kind of just fly under the radar.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.570
But when you're out there leading, when you're
out there setting the agenda, not just for

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.770
Florida, but really for the nation, which
we've.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.290
Speaker 1: Done, he's setting the agenda for
the nation.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.810
This does sound like a guy who's running.

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:36.480
Speaker 5: Over the last few years, people
see that.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.890
And the people that they don't necessarily
like that are going to respond accordingly.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:47.000
But I can just tell you, if people are not
firing at me, then I must not be doing my

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.000
job.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.710
And so I view it really as positive feedback.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.700
Well, listen, you could get some positive
feedback if you just stood up, turned around

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.079
and said, Hey, folks, I'm going to run for
president.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.149
Just saying you would wind up in a standing
ovation right now.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:00.740
We'll give you 20 seconds.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.000
You guys like to have have that announcement.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.740
I mean, it would be.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:10.479
Speaker 1: So, listen, we are going to delve
into this in a lot of different ways.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.629
But what is FOX News doing here?

00:02:12.629 --> 00:02:21.530
How does FOX News, which has been softly leaning
towards DeSantis and softly getting ready

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:27.370
to get away from Trump if Trump is not the
nominee, why don't they bring up that?

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:32.340
The lion's share of those attacks have been
coming from Donald Trump, that that's who

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.780
people are paying attention to, and we'll
have examples of it later on in today's show.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.820
Not Larry Hogan and Nikki Haley.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.500
Nobody really cares about those attacks on
DeSantis.

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:46.849
Well, it seems that it's part of the same
strategy we've seen, which is Fox would rather

00:02:46.849 --> 00:02:49.300
someone other than Trump.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.900
But if it is Trump, they don't want to openly
be hostile to him.

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:58.940
Now, Trump has already started targeting Fox
to some degree, talking about sinking ratings

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.170
and different things, but it seems part of
that same strategy.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:07.720
Fox isn't ready to abandon Trump yet, but
they do want to set themselves up to be friendly

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.720
with whoever.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.269
And so the way is you bring on DeSantis, you
ask him about the attacks on him.

00:03:14.269 --> 00:03:17.909
You just don't mention that Trump is one of
the people that's been attacking him.

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:19.970
They're creating fake.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:26.000
It's the there's constantly an elephant in
the room that people aren't mentioning.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.641
And this is the latest example of it.

00:03:27.641 --> 00:03:29.840
It's going to be a wild primary, that's for
sure.

